#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0034 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "Numeric-noise membership (VISITNUM declared Num on both sides). Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0034 (Condition VISITNUM ^= null; Rule VISITNUM in SV.VISITNUM; Description: VISITNUM must match a VISITNUM value FOR THE SUBJECT in SV). Subject 01-701-1015's SV visit is recorded as 2.0000000000001 (floating-point noise, as from a cross-platform transfer or a calculation) and the LB record carries 2. The verdict rests on the owner rulings, not on CDISC text: D81 (in IS a disjunction of ==), JCT D9 ('IN is a equals one of the following and therefore tolerance is to be considered') and D64 / JCT D8 / JCT D12 (every numeric comparison is tolerant, purely relative, by significant digits, one global default: shipped as 12 digits, eps = 2 x 10^-11 here, and |2 - 2.0000000000001| = 1e-13 is inside eps for any default up to 14 digits). So 2 == 2.0000000000001 and LB row 2 is IN its subject's SV set -> silent. The numeric-cleaning ruling (RRK E7, NCL D1: noise within 1e-12 on the decade is absorbed) gives the same answer on the text path, where the SV cell reads '2'. Today's engine reaches the silent verdict through the text path (distinct stores the cleaned text '2', and membership matches it before the tolerance arm is consulted); the rulings' target (D64h: the set keeps exact identity, tolerance at the membership comparison) gives the same verdict. Catches a port that builds typed sets and tests membership by exact key identity: 2 is not exactly 2.0000000000001, so row 2 would fire. Row 1 (01-701-1015, 1) matches exactly and is silent."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset LB class=FINDINGS label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ALB | 1 | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | LB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ALB | 2 | BASELINE
---

dataset SV label="Subject Visits"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col VISITNUM type=Num  label="Visit Number"
col VISIT    type=Char label="Visit Name"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 1               | SCREENING
CDISCPILOT01 | SV | 01-701-1015 | 2.0000000000001 | BASELINE
---
